From 18d998ebe1af122188e5b08f6904f38a0d2ec217 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Schwab <schwab@suse.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:31:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iconvdata: IBM1390/IBM1399 encoders read past input bounds
 (bug 34914)

Fix a bounds check when the IBM1390 and IBM1399 encoders look up the next
character after a combining base.

(cherry picked from commit 77fe280828e85ac329e5644e8546440e9c1b0453)
---
 NEWS                          |  3 ++
 iconvdata/Makefile            |  4 ++-
 iconvdata/ibm1364.c           |  2 +-
 iconvdata/tst-iconv-ibm1390.c | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 72 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 iconvdata/tst-iconv-ibm1390.c

diff --git a/NEWS b/NEWS
index 35f7d8648725..288d3d7f75ef 100644
--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -78,6 +78,9 @@ The following bugs are resolved with this release:
   [34875] string: 2.44 regression: Hygon non-temporal threshold can be
     zero
   [34890] malloc: free may change errno under some conditions
+  [34914] locale: iconv: IBM1390/IBM1399 encoders read up to 3 bytes
+    past the input buffer when the last complete character is a
+    combining base (CVE-2026-124024)
   [34920] math: Bug in SVE pow and powf with mixed positive and negative
     base lanes with integer exponent
   [34921] math: Bug in SVE pow and powf with mixed subnormal and
diff --git a/iconvdata/Makefile b/iconvdata/Makefile
